1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,609
Your maps have places on them.

2
00:00:03,509 --> 00:00:05,248
Today they get things:

3
00:00:05,698 --> 00:00:08,307
a locked door and its key,

4
00:00:08,757 --> 00:00:11,800
left by a tent in the yard,

5
00:00:12,250 --> 00:00:15,728
and a panel only an engineer may touch.

6
00:00:17,528 --> 00:00:22,746
Every one of them is a few lines in the fact sheet,

7
00:00:23,196 --> 00:00:27,978
and what a thing does depends on which lines it has.

8
00:00:29,178 --> 00:00:31,352
When somebody clicks a prop,

9
00:00:31,802 --> 00:00:34,846
the game asks four questions in order.

10
00:00:35,746 --> 00:00:38,789
May this person use it at all?

11
00:00:39,689 --> 00:00:42,298
Is it a door, and shut?

12
00:00:43,198 --> 00:00:45,807
Is it something to pick up?

13
00:00:46,707 --> 00:00:48,880
Does it open a scene?

14
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:53,289
It stops at the first yes.

15
00:00:53,739 --> 00:00:56,783
And if there's no yes at all,

16
00:00:57,233 --> 00:01:00,711
its description is on the handheld's Look app.

17
00:01:02,511 --> 00:01:07,728
In the game, the key lies by the foot of the tent.

18
00:01:08,178 --> 00:01:12,961
Click it, and the Pack app on the handheld has it.

19
00:01:14,761 --> 00:01:17,804
So here's the simplest prop there is.

20
00:01:18,254 --> 00:01:19,993
One line says Item,

21
00:01:20,443 --> 00:01:23,052
and a name I made up.

22
00:01:23,952 --> 00:01:28,735
Click it, and it's in your pack and off the map.

23
00:01:29,935 --> 00:01:35,587
In the game, the door stands in the gap of the pump house,

24
00:01:36,037 --> 00:01:41,254
and with the key anywhere in the party, a click opens it.

25
00:01:43,054 --> 00:01:47,837
Now the door, on the mark you painted two lectures ago.

26
00:01:48,737 --> 00:01:50,476
Blocks, and then yes,

27
00:01:50,926 --> 00:01:54,404
means nobody walks through it while it's shut.

28
00:01:55,304 --> 00:01:58,783
And Opens with lists the ways it opens,

29
00:01:59,233 --> 00:02:00,972
with commas between them.

30
00:02:02,772 --> 00:02:07,989
A key opens it when anybody in the party is carrying one,

31
00:02:08,439 --> 00:02:11,483
not just the one at the door.

32
00:02:12,383 --> 00:02:14,557
A check is a roll:

33
00:02:15,007 --> 00:02:19,354
a ten sided die, plus a skill, against a number.

34
00:02:20,254 --> 00:02:23,733
And cut means a shot from the weapon.

35
00:02:25,533 --> 00:02:27,272
Two warnings about checks.

36
00:02:28,172 --> 00:02:29,911
Write the key first,

37
00:02:30,361 --> 00:02:33,404
because the terms are tried in order.

38
00:02:34,304 --> 00:02:38,217
And a check can be tried again at once,

39
00:02:38,667 --> 00:02:44,754
so a door with a check on it will always open in the end.

40
00:02:45,954 --> 00:02:49,433
Here are the next two in the game.

41
00:02:50,333 --> 00:02:54,246
After the toolbox, the Pack app reads two fuses,

42
00:02:54,696 --> 00:02:58,609
and the notice opens a scene on the handheld.

43
00:03:00,409 --> 00:03:03,452
The toolbox is a pickup worth two.

44
00:03:03,902 --> 00:03:06,511
That's the line that says Qty.

45
00:03:08,311 --> 00:03:10,485
The notice opens a scene.

46
00:03:10,935 --> 00:03:13,978
Scene, and the key of a room,

47
00:03:14,428 --> 00:03:18,341
the same join you saw on the starter's terminal.

48
00:03:19,241 --> 00:03:21,850
And it has one more line:

49
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:24,039
Once, and then yes.

50
00:03:24,939 --> 00:03:27,548
The room opens the first time.

51
00:03:28,448 --> 00:03:32,796
After that a click only walks you up to it,

52
00:03:33,246 --> 00:03:36,724
and its description is on the Look app.

53
00:03:38,524 --> 00:03:40,698
Be careful with that one.

54
00:03:41,148 --> 00:03:43,322
It counts the room opening,

55
00:03:43,772 --> 00:03:45,511
not what anyone answered.

56
00:03:46,711 --> 00:03:50,624
In the game, the doctor clicks the pump panel,

57
00:03:51,074 --> 00:03:54,987
and the Look app tells her she'd need engineering.

58
00:03:56,787 --> 00:03:59,830
The pump panel is a terminal too,

59
00:04:00,280 --> 00:04:02,020
with one new line.

60
00:04:02,920 --> 00:04:04,659
Needs, and a job.

61
00:04:06,459 --> 00:04:10,807
Anyone else who clicks it is told they'd need engineering,

62
00:04:11,257 --> 00:04:12,996
and gets nothing more.

63
00:04:13,896 --> 00:04:17,374
That's stricter than a choice in a room.

64
00:04:17,824 --> 00:04:22,607
A choice for a missing job gets covered by somebody else.

65
00:04:23,057 --> 00:04:25,230
Nobody covers for a Needs.

66
00:04:27,030 --> 00:04:31,813
So never put the only way through your story behind one.

67
00:04:32,713 --> 00:04:34,887
Scan is the simple one.

68
00:04:35,337 --> 00:04:38,815
It's what the scanner says about the thing,

69
00:04:39,265 --> 00:04:42,309
when a crew member can see it.

70
00:04:43,509 --> 00:04:47,422
Three short rooms at the end of the file.

71
00:04:47,872 --> 00:04:50,480
You know how to write these.

72
00:04:51,380 --> 00:04:53,554
The notice teaches a fact.

73
00:04:54,454 --> 00:04:57,498
And the lever's answer sends a signal.

74
00:04:59,298 --> 00:05:02,341
Lint warns that nothing hears that signal.

75
00:05:02,791 --> 00:05:04,965
That's true for the moment.

76
00:05:05,415 --> 00:05:08,459
The next step is what hears it.

77
00:05:09,659 --> 00:05:13,572
Downstairs in the game, walk east along the walkway,

78
00:05:14,022 --> 00:05:18,370
and the gate comes into view, shut across the way.

79
00:05:19,270 --> 00:05:22,313
The gauge stands out in the water.

80
00:05:24,113 --> 00:05:26,722
Three marks in the cistern first,

81
00:05:27,172 --> 00:05:30,650
one new legend line and one click each.

82
00:05:32,450 --> 00:05:37,667
The sluice gate is a door with only one way to open.

83
00:05:38,117 --> 00:05:40,726
Opens with, signal, and a name.

84
00:05:41,626 --> 00:05:44,670
Nobody on the ground can force it.

85
00:05:45,570 --> 00:05:48,178
The spare cell says Hidden until,

86
00:05:48,628 --> 00:05:50,367
and the same name.

87
00:05:50,817 --> 00:05:56,035
It isn't on the map at all until that signal is sent.

88
00:05:57,835 --> 00:06:02,617
So one answer in the pump house does two things downstairs.

89
00:06:03,067 --> 00:06:04,807
It opens the gate,

90
00:06:05,257 --> 00:06:07,430
and it uncovers the cell.

91
00:06:09,230 --> 00:06:13,143
The gauge is out of reach in the water.

92
00:06:13,593 --> 00:06:15,767
Reach, and the number two,

93
00:06:16,217 --> 00:06:20,565
lets a crew member use it from two cells away.

94
00:06:21,465 --> 00:06:24,943
On the walkway, the Look app offers it.

95
00:06:26,743 --> 00:06:28,917
And lint is clean again,

96
00:06:29,367 --> 00:06:31,976
because something hears the signal now.

97
00:06:33,176 --> 00:06:35,350
A word before you play.

98
00:06:36,250 --> 00:06:38,424
Lint reads a door now.

99
00:06:39,324 --> 00:06:42,367
Misspell the key's name, or the signal's,

100
00:06:42,817 --> 00:06:46,296
and it tells you nothing gives that key,

101
00:06:46,746 --> 00:06:48,920
or nothing sends that signal.

102
00:06:50,720 --> 00:06:54,198
What it can't check is the skill's name,

103
00:06:54,648 --> 00:06:58,126
or the order you wrote the ways in.

104
00:06:59,026 --> 00:07:01,635
So check those with a pencil.

105
00:07:03,435 --> 00:07:06,043
Then play it with two consoles.

106
00:07:06,943 --> 00:07:09,117
The doctor carries the key,

107
00:07:09,567 --> 00:07:12,176
and the engineer opens the door.

108
00:07:13,076 --> 00:07:17,424
The doctor can't work the panel, and the engineer can.

109
00:07:19,224 --> 00:07:24,876
For the exercise, add a second key somewhere it can never be reached,

110
00:07:25,326 --> 00:07:27,935
and say why that's a mistake.

111
00:07:29,735 --> 00:07:32,343
Next time, somebody to talk to,

112
00:07:32,793 --> 00:07:34,533
and something that bites.
